### ==========================================
### SUPPORT DESK TICKET API SECURITY TESTS
### ==========================================

### 1. Health endpoint is public (Should return 200 OK)
GET http://localhost:8082/api/health


### 2. Ticket endpoint without token returns 401
GET http://localhost:8082/api/tickets


### 3. Register user returns token (Should return 201 Created)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Alice",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "mySecurePassword123"
}


### 4. Login user returns token (Should return 200 OK)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "mySecurePassword123"
}


### 5. Ticket endpoint with token returns 200
GET http://localhost:8082/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}


### 6. Create ticket with normal USER token returns 403
POST http://localhost:8082/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}

{
  "title": "Broken Screen",
  "description": "The monitor in lab 3 is flashing green.",
  "category": "Software",
  "priority": "Medium",
  "status": "Open",
  "createdBy": "Alice"
}


### 7. Login admin returns token (Should return 200 OK)
POST http://localhost:8082/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Admin@12345"
}


### 8. Create ticket with ADMIN token returns 201
POST http://localhost:8082/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "title": "Server Outage",
  "description": "Production database is not responding to connections.",
  "category": "Database",
  "priority": "Critical",
  "status": "Open",
  "createdBy": "Jason"
}